was renamed to that from krea2-concept-sliders. This notice applies
either way.

This repository does not contain Krea 2 weights, the
jimmycarter/krea2-turbo-bbox transformer, the Comfy single-file
safetensors, or any trained slider. Those files stay on Hugging Face.

jimmycarter/krea2-turbo-bbox is a finetune of krea/Krea-2-Raw merged
with the Krea-2 Turbo distillation delta. Use of that model and of
krea/Krea-2-Raw is governed by the Krea 2 Community License published
with the weights, not by the MIT license on this code:

https://huggingface.co/jimmycarter/krea2-turbo-bbox/blob/main/LICENSE.md

The stock text encoder and VAE used at inference
(qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors and qwen_image_vae.safetensors)
come from Comfy-Org/Krea-2 and are separate downloads.

A slider trained on this base is a derivative of the Krea model.
Shipping it later does not relicense the weights as MIT. Say which
epoch subfolder it was trained on, and keep the Krea license notice
with the adapter.
